Kept: the app — its name, release history and release images (not billed) — so
  `forge env deploy <env> <release>` recreates an env; custom domains stay in your organization, unbound.
Each env's secrets stop being delivered and are not given back to a recreated env: set them again.
Afterwards nothing runs or bills except the kept databases' storage.

  prod     deleted; the platform is tearing it down
  staging  deleted; the platform is tearing it down

Tore down app "shop": every env is deleted and the platform is tearing them down. Its releases are kept.
Kept databases bill storage until purged: `forge env retained list`, then `forge env retained purge <id>`.
